@{
    ViewBag.Title = "About";
}

<div class="kpi-page-head">
    <div>
        <h2>About</h2>
        <p class="kpi-subtitle">@ViewBag.Message</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="kpi-panel">
    <h3>What this system does</h3>
    <p>
        The HR KPI Monitoring System pulls the monthly KPI figures already produced by the
        source HR system, validates and loads them through an ETL pipeline, compares each one
        against its target, and publishes the result to this dashboard. The figures are never
        recalculated here, so the dashboard and the source system always agree.
    </p>

    <h3>Data flow</h3>
    <p>
        Source KPI system &rarr; staging &rarr; core tables &rarr; reporting views &rarr; dashboard and exports.
        Only the reporting layer is exposed to the web application, which keeps the raw data
        out of reach of the site.
    </p>

    <h3>Access</h3>
    <p>
        Access is controlled per role. A viewer is bound to a single department; managers and
        administrators can switch between departments and export the full breakdown. Logins,
        denied access attempts and exports are recorded in the audit log.
    </p>
</div>
